  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This dataset is showing early but tangible uptake: it has been downloaded 1,202 times, cited 2 times in OpenAlex, and documented as reused in 2 downstream works. The record points to active interest in open access publishing trends, while still remaining a small citation base.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Ulrich Herb\u2019s dataset, published in 2025 on Zenodo, compiles Open Access publishing trends for journal articles from 2015 to 2024 using OpenAlex data. Its strongest impact signal is usage: more than a thousand downloads indicate that the resource is being consulted rather than simply archived.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Scholarly uptake is present but still early. OpenAlex records 2 citations, both appearing in 2026, and the citing works are in a narrow thematic area centered on academic publishing, open access, research data management, and digital education. That pattern suggests the dataset is already being drawn into adjacent discussions about scholarly communication and open science.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">There is also evidence of downstream reuse. Two documented reuses are recorded, and Crossref data-citation tracking shows the dataset being referenced explicitly as a dataset in two posted-content works. Together, these signals show that the resource is not only being read, but also incorporated into subsequent outputs.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The surrounding record is otherwise quiet. No event-data mentions or scite citation classifications are available, and public-discourse tracking is unavailable from the archive. Overall, this is a dataset with clear signs of practical use and emerging scholarly relevance, but the evidence base is still modest and best read as an early uptake profile rather than a mature citation story.</p>",
